Paid plans. The plugin is on the account: every device signed in to it gets it.

+ Sidebar: *Plugins* → *Add* → *Add custom MCP server*

  #image("assets/chatgpt_plugins_add.png")
+ Name: `Service Arb`, or your own. Description: what it covers, so ChatGPT knows when to use it. URL: `https://sa.evinvest.ltd/playbook_mcp`. Authentication: *OAuth*. Tick *I understand and want to continue*, then *Create as a plugin*, and sign in.

  #image("assets/chatgpt_custom_mcp.png", width: 50%)
+ Where the plan has Skills (Business, Enterprise, Edu): download #link("https://github.com/EV-Service-Arb/playbook/releases/download/service-arb-skill/service-arb.zip")[service-arb.zip], then *Plugins* → *Skills* → *Create* → *Upload from your computer*. A newer zip replaces it the same way.
+ In a chat: *+* → *Service Arb*. To keep it off the web, say so: "answer only from service-arb".

  #image("assets/chatgpt_chat_plus.png", width: 60%)

Without Skills, ChatGPT has the server's tools but not the skill that says how to answer from them: answers drift further from the sources than in the other clients.

Sign in again: *Connect* on the plugin.
